# Two cards put into graveyards at the same time, each triggering the Void: Wrath of God destroys an Ornithopter of each
# player together, and the Void (an enchantment, so it stays) exiles both and then the Wrath itself. The positive control of
# planar-void-destroyed-with-a-creature-exiles-neither, which is the same game with the Void among the casualties.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Planar Void
Ornithopter
Swamp x4
Swamp x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Plains
Plains
Wrath of God
Ornithopter
Island
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Planar Void.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Wrath of God.Cast
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = Ornithopter; Ornithopter; Wrath of God
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Swamp; Planar Void
